 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "sotah.36a.11",
   "daf": "36a",
   "sentenceId": 10,
   "he": "שִׁשָּׁה שְׁבָטִים עָלוּ לְרֹאשׁ הַר גְּרִיזִים כּוּ׳. מַאי ״וְהַחֶצְיוֹ״? אָמַר רַב כָּהֲנָא: כְּדֶרֶךְ שֶׁחֲלוּקִין כָּאן — כָּךְ חֲלוּקִין בְּאַבְנֵי אֵפוֹד.",
   "en": "§ It is stated in the mishna: «Six tribes ascended to the top of Mount Gerizim,» as it is stated: “Half of them in front of Mount Gerizim and the half of them in front of Mount Ebal” (Joshua 8:33). The Gemara asks: «What» is the meaning of the term «“and the half of them”?» It seems to be referring to a division that already existed. «Rav Kahana says: The same way that» the tribes «were divided up here» on the mountains, «so» too «were they divided on the stones of the ephod,» a garment of the High Priest."
  }
 ],
